Since April, the desk has merged 412 unique reports about dates into #4471. The export contains
427 rows because some reports appear more than once; count each report ID once.

The reports describe two problems, not one. The shared parser read month first for day-first
tenants. Separately, booking-v3 told people to enter month first even when their tenant's date
format was day first. The parser is fixed. The hint issue will not be fixed because booking-v3
has been retired.

<Callout>
Desk update: #4471 closed 5 October. Parser fix shipped; booking-v3 hint issue won't be fixed.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The cause comes from the tenant's locale, form version, and report channel, not the intake tag.
Intake tagged 371 reports `parser` and 41 `hint`; those guesses do not define the cause. The five
reports noted as one-day moves remain in the parser group because their tenants use day-first
dates and they did not come through booking-v3. The 379 parser reports map to the shipped fix;
the 33 hint reports map to the retired form and a won't-fix outcome.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- A large ticket can hide multiple causes. Group by product behavior, not by symptom or intake tag.
- Deduplicate by report ID before counting: overlapping export pages are not extra reports.
- Keep the one-day-move notes visible without treating those reports as a third cause.

